Driving method
--------------
1. Asset IMPORT: real UI file input (`<input type=file>` under the Assets
   panel, NOT the reference-media input under Generate) driven by
   constructing a File from the fetched fixture bytes and dispatching a
   real `change` event — equivalent to what Playwright's `setFiles()` does
   under the hood. Verified via editor.media.getAssets() → asset landed
   with name "audio_only_3s.m4a", type "audio", duration 3.
2. Timeline placement (SEEDING via bridge, per worker instructions):
   editor.timeline.insertElement() with volume:1, muted:false — the same
   command-stack seam e2e/export-fidelity/helpers.ts's insertAudioElement
   uses. This only PLACES the clip; it does not touch volume for the test.
3. Selection: editor.selection.setSelectedElements({elements: [{trackId,
   elementId}]}) — the correct call shape per src/core/managers/
   selection-manager.ts (setSelectedElements({elements}): ElementRef[]).
   NOTE: an earlier attempt called setSelectedElements([elementId]) (wrong
   shape — raw array of a string ID instead of {elements: ElementRef[]})
   and crashed the whole editor ("The editor hit an unexpected error") via
   a TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'length') in
   useTransformHandles (src/hooks/use-transform-handles.ts:137,
   `selectedElements.length === 1`), because getSelectedElements() then
   returned undefined. This is NOT filed as a product bug — it was this
   worker's own misuse of an internal, non-UI-exposed API with the wrong
   argument shape, not something reachable through the real UI (a real
   click-to-select always goes through the correctly-typed call). Recorded
   here only so the false lead isn't rediscovered. Reloading the editor and
   calling the API correctly did not reproduce the crash.
4. Volume set to 0.5: REAL UI — typed "50" into the actual Properties-panel
   Volume "Level" NumberField textbox (ref resolved via accessibility tree,
   filled via form_input, which fills the real DOM textbox) that a human
   user would use. Panel showed "+0.0 dB" -> "-6.0 dB", "100%" -> "50%"
   confirming the real UI reflected the change; editor.timeline state
   confirmed element.volume === 0.5 afterward.
5. Export: REAL UI — clicked the real "Export" button (top bar), the real
   export dialog opened (platform presets, format radio group, quality
   radio group, "Include audio in export" / "Include Byorn watermark"
   checkboxes, real "Export" submit button inside the dialog). Selected the
   "Podcast (audio only)" preset (content is audio-only) and clicked the
   dialog's "Export" button. This is the same button/dialog a paying user
   drives — NOT the E2E stub (E2E_STUB_EXPORT=0 for this whole build, and
   the E2EBridge's real-export tap in e2e-bridge.tsx confirms this by
   exposing genuine getLastExportResult() from the real renderer.exportProject).

